-- The 3450 weapons and pieces of armour that upstream has no disenchant id for.
--
-- After restoring the 8404 values sql/base does carry, this many uncommon-and-
-- better items still had none - 2070 of them Turtle's own additions above entry
-- 30000 - and an item with no id cannot be disenchanted at all.
--
-- The mapping is not remembered, it is read off the restored data: the majority
-- disenchant id per quality, item class and five-point item level band, across
-- those 8939 known-good rows. Majorities run from 71% to 100%, mostly above 80.
-- It comes out as the familiar vanilla table - uncommon armour on templates 1 to
-- 11, uncommon weapons on 21 to 31, rare on 41 to 49 and epic on 61 to 65, both
-- classes sharing the last two.
--
-- Three bands had no evidence and continue the series downward: uncommon weapons
-- below item level 6, rare below 16, epic below 41. Upstream has nothing there, so
-- the lowest tier applies.
--
-- 49 items carry item level 0. For those the required level is used instead, and
-- where that is also 0 they land in the lowest band. An epic at item level 0 is a
-- data oddity either way.
--
-- Only rows still holding 0 are touched.


